There's no reason to "get rid of pudding farming".  If you're going to
have monsters that can split endlessly (ie: don't respect extinction),
then you need to realize that it is going to be possible to "abuse"
this- except it's not really abuse.

Pudding farming is no different than running in circles for a couple
hours fighting random battles to level up in a console RPG- it's a task
that's done solely for the improvement of your character and has no
relevant to the plot/progression of the game.

People should stop complaining about pudding farming- any game that has
the depth of Nethack is going to have things like pudding farming.
Just accept it as a part of the game and move on.  If you get rid of
pudding farming, people will just do something else instead. (daytime
gremlin farming anyone?)

It seems that every group of gamers has a subgroup that feels the need
to complain about anything that's a good play and calls it cheap, and
refuses to do it.  If it only went this far, it wouldn't be a problem-
it's when that group starts criticizing everyone who actually utilizes
all the tools in the game that it's a problem.  Take fighting games,
for instance- there's always some group of players who consider throws
"cheap", or considers some specific character "cheap" and refuse to
play as that character or use throws- that's not a problem, you can
play the game however you want. Of course, not using the best stuff
available to you in something such as a tournament is obviously bad
play, and you will/should lose for that.  The problem comes when,
instead of becoming a better player and using the throws, you whine,
bitch, and moan, and complain about people who DO play well and use all
the tools available to them as a player. Even worse are those who claim
that those who do use the tools are cheating, when it's clearly a part
of the game.  Someone in #nethack on freenode was claiming that anyone
who uses #name (heart of ahriman) on a gray stone to see if it's a
luckstone is cheating. This is clearly preposterous.


Sure, pudding farming means the high score won't be accomplished
through normal playing, but let's face it- no matter what you do, the
high score won't be accomplished "normally"- you have to do something
out of the ordinary, since you're playing for score and not just
beating the game.



